{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1325827-character-creation-encourages-early-min-max","id":1325827,"title":"Character Creation encourages early min-max?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-18T19:47:37-07:00","id":1325827,"title":"Character Creation encourages early min-max?","content":"If I understand Trinity Core right, at character creation I get a free Specialty for each skill at 3, but after character creation I have to spend xp on them?<br /> <br /> Doesn't this just encourage players to stack their skills as much as possible.. everyone will just hyper specialize at character creation??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25494-robskylor","name":"Robskylor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T19:58:37-07:00","id":1325831,"title":"","content":"In part that\u2019s the point. You create a character that works well in a team. That\u2019s the same thing for the CP costs that don\u2019t scale up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T20:28:56-07:00","id":1325839,"title":"","content":"It could be argued that you always get a free one when you hit 3 in an ability, and that additional specialties cost XP. It doesn't say that you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T20:38:48-07:00","id":1325847,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25494-robskylor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25494_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25494\" data-vbnamecard=\"25494\">Robskylor</a> Specialties are nice, but they're not all that. I really didn't bother fishing for them when I made the character I'm currently playing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> I like the way you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T21:15:25-07:00","id":1325863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1325827-character-creation-encourages-early-min-max?p=1325847#post1325847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25494-robskylor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25494_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25494\" data-vbnamecard=\"25494\">Robskylor</a> Specialties are nice, but they're not all that. I really didn't bother fishing for them when I made the character I'm currently playing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> I like the way you think.</div> </div> </div> </div>My notion has always been to read ambiguous rules in the most beneficial-to-me way. That's why &quot;Current Rating * X&quot; means the current rating, multiplied by whatever. Not, as a dev once said was intended, &quot;The rating you're currently buying&quot; multiplied by whatever :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T23:48:39-07:00","id":1325895,"title":"","content":"It's also worth remembering that having a few bad dice pools is actually good for you. Failing rolls is a good way to build Momentum, so more specialized characters (I somewhat reject the min-max concept because it implies a level of optimization that's not really going to matter here) have some low dice pools that are likely to fail around to help them in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:44:14-07:00","id":1325946,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> That's a fair point, it is kinda ambiguous about that. I'd be curious to ask a Dev if there's always a free Specialty or not. That's how I might have to run it either way tho.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I hadn't considered that. I like it. Just started looking into this system, getting my head wrapped around some of the newer concepts.<br /> <br /> I acknowledge it's not that big of a deal, I was glad to see that they got rid of the &quot;Current rating&quot; or &quot;next rating&quot; from previous White Wolf games. The nature of the character creation process heavily incentivized a hyper specialized build. Granted I've got a pretty good crew that makes the characters they want rather the most powerful. But it's still poor game design to mechanically punish folks for making well rounded characters.<br /> <br /> With Trinity just having dots of the same type cost the same whether it's lvl 2 or lvl 5, it solves that problem. The Specialty thing just stood out to me as the only remnant of the old problem. A minor gripe, only a big deal because it's the only real flaw I see. Kinda like a single scratch on your new car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25494,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25494-robskylor","user":"Robskylor","date":". 07-21-2019, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25494-robskylor","name":"Robskylor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}